    },
    "message": "fix(request-log): stop claiming compaction widens the page size\n\nCompaction set PRAGMA page_size before its VACUUM. SQLite refuses to\nchange page size on a WAL database, so the pragma was silently ignored:\nthe real log came out of compaction still at 4,096 bytes while the code,\nthe release notes and the docs all said 16 KB.\n\nCaught by printing page_size after compacting the live database rather\nthan trusting the code that set it.\n\nHonouring the claim would mean dropping out of WAL around the vacuum and\nback afterwards. That is a real risk to take on someone's only copy of\ntheir history in exchange for an uncertain few percent, so the claim goes\ninstead. Everything the compaction actually does is unchanged: 1.73 GB to\n0.29 GB on the live log, all 50,034 bodies verified against a backup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
